Z||000038||BN Boomer||08-23-99||10:44 PM||||My guess is that the pulley below the alternator is attached to a power steering pump.
Z||000039||mwbackus||08-23-99||11:03 PM||||You really can not see the exhaust manifolds well in the above pic.  The front manifold uses a crossover pipe that extends under the front of the motor to the rear manifold.  Both exhausts exit from the turbo via one pipe in nearly the same location as the 2.8 rear manifold.  It also seems likely that these manifolds could be used on a NA 4.3 by using an adapter for connection to the turbo mount flange(instead of a turbo).  A better illustration of the manifold system can be found here :<br>http://www.syty.org/pics/diagrams/enginebay-small.gif<p>Mike
Z||000040||mwbackus||08-23-99||11:08 PM||||Power steering?? Whats that?  You are obviously correct. :-)  So if the PS pump was to removed, I would guess that it would be possible to relocate the alternator to that area.  The alternator seems to be the only real obstacle that would prevent this motor from working in the Fiero engine bay.<p>Mike
Z||000041||lowCG||08-24-99||12:50 AM||||Yeah,if it's not a pancake style PS pump,you could always run the alternator off the final drive(machine a groove in the flange).
Z||000042||Phil||08-24-99||04:49 AM||||I see the question of mufflers came up. I'm redoing my muffler system-- well really I'm fitting some type of muffler system on. I have a S/C 3800 conversion and my only mufflers are resonator tips(very loud). Checked into Supertrapps ($166 ea.)I finally found a guy who hot rods Saabs and on one he had used Supertrapps then changed it over to Hooker muffler tips ($122). He liked them much better they were cheaper, quiter and cleaner (Supertrapps throw the exhaust perpendicular to the pipe and get your bumper dirty). The Hookers are 10" long 4" dia. and fit 2 1/4 and 2 1/2 pipes
Z||000043||batboy||08-24-99||07:12 AM||||Thanks for the info Phil. It's funny that you mention Hooker, I've been looking at their resonator tips in the JEGS catalog which sale for $30 a piece. I figure I didn't need the full muffler tips since I already have glass packs which will evenually be swapped for Flowmaster mufflers. I heard that for the price, Hooker is pretty good.<p>Squid, since I'm spending a grand on Dart aluminum heads, I guess I can spend a couple hundred more for the ceramic coated headers. You're right, they would work better than the insulation wrap, thanks for the tip.
